Creates the `Intl.Segmenter` and the `\p{RGI_Emoji}` regex on the first call instead of on import.
Together they take ~14 ms, which every import of `utilery` and `utilery/string` paid, even when
`getStringWidth` and `wrapText` are never called. The regex is built with the constructor: V8 checks
regex literals while parsing the file, so a literal costs as much even inside a function that never runs.

